# Operators and edits on closed folds, and folds following edits around them.

=== dd on a closed fold deletes all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>dd
expect:
  one
  |five
regs:   "" = "two\nthree\nfour\n"   "1 = "two\nthree\nfour\n"

=== yy on a closed fold yanks all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>yy
expect:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
regs:   "" = "two\nthree\n"   "0 = "two\nthree\n"

=== >> on a closed fold shifts all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :set sw=2 et<CR>:2,3fold<CR>>>
expect:
  one
  |  two
    three
  four

=== cc on a closed fold replaces all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>ccX<Esc>
expect:
  one
  |X
  four

=== x on a closed fold deletes the whole fold
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  Thus "dl" deletes the whole closed fold under the cursor.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>x
expect:
  one
  |four
regs:   "" = "two\nthree\n"

=== dj from a closed fold deletes the fold and the next line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>dj
expect:
  one
  |five

=== dk onto a closed fold deletes the whole fold
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
  five
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>dk
expect:
  one
  |five

=== 2dd on a closed fold counts it as one line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>2dd
expect:
  one
  |five

=== g~~ on a closed fold changes case in all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>g~~
expect:
  one
  |TWO
  THREE
  four

=== p on a closed fold puts after its last line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>yyjp
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  |one
  four

=== P on a closed fold puts before its first line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  two
  three
  |four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>yykP
expect:
  one
  |four
  two
  three
  four

=== o on a closed fold opens a line after the fold
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>onew<Esc>
expect:
  one
  two
  three
  ne|w
  four

=== :s on a closed fold works on all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  when used with the cursor on a closed fold, will replace "foo" with "bar" in all lines of the fold.
given:
  foo
  |foo
  foo
  foo
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>:s/foo/bar/<CR>
expect:
  foo
  bar
  |bar
  foo

=== :d on a closed fold deletes all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  For Ex commands that operate on buffer lines, the range is adjusted to always start at the first line of a closed fold and end at the last line of a closed fold.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>:d<CR>
expect:
  one
  |four

=== dd on an open fold deletes one line
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>zodd
expect:
  one
  |three
  four

=== u after dd on a closed fold restores all its lines
ref:    fold.txt *fold-behavior*
quote:  When using an operator, a closed fold is included as a whole.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>dd
expect:
  one
  |four
undo:
  one
  |two
  three
  four

=== a line inserted above moves the fold down
ref:    fold.txt *fold-manual*
quote:  Use commands to manually define the fold regions.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>Onew<Esc>jjj
expect:
  new
  one
  two
  three
  fo|ur

=== a line deleted above moves the fold up
ref:    fold.txt *fold-manual*
quote:  Use commands to manually define the fold regions.
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>ddj
expect:
  two
  three
  |four

=== a line added inside an open fold extends it
ref:    fold.txt *fold-manual*
quote:  Use commands to manually define the fold regions.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
keys:   :2,3fold<CR>zoonew<Esc>zcj
expect:
  one
  two
  new
  three
  fo|ur

=== a line deleted inside an open fold shrinks it
ref:    fold.txt *fold-manual*
quote:  Use commands to manually define the fold regions.
given:
  one
  |two
  three
  four
  five
keys:   :2,4fold<CR>zojddzcj
expect:
  one
  two
  four
  |five
